From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:21:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: allow disabling automatic shared GPIO ownership

The downstream Spectra camera driver, which AGNOS builds as an
out-of-tree module, arbitrates the shared camera GPIOs itself through
the legacy integer API. With GPIO_SHARED, gpiolib reserves GPIOs
referenced by multiple firmware consumers for its shared GPIO proxies,
so every sensor power-up fails with EBUSY before Spectra can acquire
them.

Expose the existing setting to expert configurations, so that AGNOS can
turn it off and leave the GPIO ownership to Spectra. Keep automatic
sharing enabled by default.

This is local to AGNOS and goes away with the Spectra driver.

Signed-off-by: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpio/Kconfig | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
index a48586bb8e..e16250d4fc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
@@ -46,9 +46,15 @@ config GPIOLIB_IRQCHIP
 	bool
 
 config GPIO_SHARED
-	def_bool y
+	bool "Automatic shared GPIO ownership" if EXPERT
+	default y
 	depends on HAVE_SHARED_GPIOS || COMPILE_TEST
 	select AUXILIARY_BUS
+	help
+	  Automatically reserve GPIOs referenced by multiple firmware consumers
+	  and arbitrate their values through shared GPIO proxies. Disable this
+	  when legacy GPIO consumers already manage ownership of shared lines.
+	  If unsure, say Y.
 
 config DEBUG_GPIO
 	bool "Debug GPIO calls"
